# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Go reference source — pinned shallow clone, never vendored into history.
# The pinned SHA is recorded in MIGRATION.md; re-clone from there.
#
# **No trailing slash, on purpose.** `/reference/mattermost/` matches only a directory, and in a
# worktree this path is a *symlink* to the main checkout's clone. On 2026-09-13 a `git add -A` in
# a worktree therefore committed both symlinks, and merging that into main clobbered the real
# clone and the whole build directory (git treats ignored paths as expendable when a tracked
# file lands on them). The same for `.build`, which was never listed at all.
/reference/mattermost
/reference/.build

# Local environment
.env
.env.local

# SQLx offline query cache is intentionally NOT ignored — commit .sqlx/
# so compile-time query verification works without a live database.

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Agent tooling. CLAUDE.md is the checked-in contributor contract and stays tracked;
# .claude/ is per-machine harness config (permissions, hooks) with no bearing on the port.
# Ignored whole so `git status` stays a signal — an unexpected entry there is meant to mean
# something, per the fixture-generator rule in README.md.
.claude/

# Compiled fixture generator (go build ./... in reference/dump drops it here).
/reference/dump/dump
__pycache__/

# The Go server built from the pinned SHA, plus its runtime root. Rebuilt by
# scripts/go-server.sh; never committed.
/reference/.build/

# A worktree pins itself to a stack with this file; see scripts/worktree.sh.
.mmrs-stack
